{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>לא</b> — It speaks of thought, for it is in the forehead." "<b>עשה</b> — like: עשות ספרים (the making of books)." "<b>סטים</b> — acts of crookedness, from the root of כי תשטה אשתו (when a wife goes astray); לא ידבק בי סטות (let no crookedness cling to me)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 101, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is elliptical; 'it is in the forehead' likely refers to a facial expression revealing intent, rendered hyper-literally.", 2 "Resolved ע\"מ as עלילות מרמה or similar; taken here as 'acts of crookedness/deceit' based on context and the cited root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:41.782371181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}